PCM clients no longer hang or die on the control socket: upstream 916c50f and 5f3eeef (both v4.2.0), backported to 4.0.0.
The ALSA plugin (and bluealsa-cli) send Drain/Drop/Pause/Resume over the PCM control socket and
then wait for the reply with poll(..., -1): an app froze for good if the daemon never answered, and
write() on a socket the daemon had closed (daemon stopped or restarted) raised SIGPIPE and killed it.
- 916c50f "Protect PCM client control socket from SIGPIPE": send(..., MSG_NOSIGNAL). Taken as is.
- 5f3eeef "Do not block forever PCM client on control command": the reply wait is bounded, 3000 ms
  for Drain and 200 ms for Drop, Pause and Resume, and a timeout fails the command with EIO. Taken
  as is; 4.0.0's one direct caller (bluealsa_pause() in bluealsa-pcm.c) passes 200 like upstream's.
